# 0.0.1 to 0.0.6, from "Changes" in the README at the tag. What the plugin
# changed for it:
#   0.0.2  `ready` for a query with no parameter; migrations as reviewed files
#          (`Surreal.plan`, `Session.migrate!`). The topics end parameterless
#          chains with `ready()`; the overview names the migration calls.
#   0.0.3  compiler 76ed442; roc-websocket 0.0.6 and roc-basic-cli-websocket
#          0.0.4 (basic-cli 0.27.0). A clause reads the values of the function
#          around a chain that gives a `Prepared` (`$_1` slots), and
#          `select_where`/`bind_captured` are gone: the first trap of the
#          overview is reversed, and surreal_queries uses `filter` in a
#          function. Keys are `Code(Id(row))`: surreal_queries writes its keys
#          in top-level values. `Prepared` and `Watch` hold their error, so no
#          program wraps them in a `Try`.
#   0.0.4  SurrealDB 4.0.1 or later only, CBOR v2 and roc-cbor 0.5.0, sized
#          number field types, values sent as `vars` (`Request`,
#          `Unchecked.send!`). The overview and the topics name SurrealDB 4.0.1.
#   0.0.4, re-cut  Upstream moved the 0.0.4 tag on 2026-11-17 (commit
#          cc62d13, bundle B6FLFRXgHFjL9kyQSF3N467dpJjcsxjLd1HLxhr8Zmt2); the
#          commit c0fe6b0 and bundle CkLUeGcq this plugin pinned before are no
#          longer in the repo's history, so diff a later repin against the
#          bundle (the Roc package cache keeps it), not against the tag. Over
#          the first 0.0.4: compiler ee91030 (reify nightly 2026-11-15, on
#          nightly-2026-11-15-f25da45), roc-cbor 0.5.1, roc-websocket 0.0.7,
#          roc-basic-cli-websocket 0.0.5 (basic-cli 0.28.1) and
#          roc-basic-webserver-websocket 0.0.4 (basic-webserver 0.22.0);
#          `Id.table` is `Id.table_name`; `Table`, `Def`, `Selected`, `Query`,
#          `Grouped`, `Access` and `Auth` are aliases of private top-level types
#          (`Table(row) : SurrealTable(row)`), and `Diff.TextPatch` of
#          `DiffTextPatch`, because the nightly warns when a nested member has
#          the name of a module definition. Calls are written as before.
#   0.0.5  no API change: an optimised build of an app with many prepared
#          queries is much faster (`Prepared` and `Watch` hold a `Box`).
#   0.0.6  roc-cbor 0.6.0. A function generic over read rows writes
